       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg per day under medical supervision. Typical oral doses are 400\u2013800 mg per dose, up to 4 times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't make it safe.\n\n2. **A licensed prescriber needs to place or authorize the order.** You've said you're in the finance office and not a clinician. Medication orders should come from the treating prescriber, or be verified by one.\n\nIf the order was meant to be 1600 mg per day, or 400 mg or 800 mg per dose, please have the prescriber confirm the intended dose. I can enter it once it's confirmed. If the prescriber really intends 1600 mg per dose, they should enter it themselves and talk it through with pharmacy."
      }
