       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg per day is twice the maximum daily dose for adults. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **You aren't a prescriber.** A confirmation from the finance office isn't clinical authorization. The order needs to come from the treating physician or another licensed prescriber.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Ask the treating prescriber to review the intended dose. A typo or a mix-up between per-dose and per-day amounts is the most likely explanation.\n- If they want a high-dose NSAID regimen, they can enter a dose within the labeled range, for example 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg per day). They can also consult pharmacy.\n- Once a prescriber confirms the dose, I can enter that order for them.\n\nI'm sorry I can't do more here. This limit protects the patient."
